SECTION 1: CORE STABILIZATION DEMONSTRATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

This section demonstrates the fundamental ΦπεNode stabilization formula:
    
    Stabilized = (ψ + φ) * (1 - ε)
    
Where:
    ψ (psi)     = Recursive animation signal (charge-based)
    φ (phi)     = Harmonic equilibrium state (tension-based)
    ε (epsilon) = Incremental drift/error (depth-based)
    Σ (sigma)   = Stabilization coexistence operator


--- Initialize Base State ---
Φ 5.0          # Set tension (phi_state) to 5.0
Ψ 3.0          # Set charge (psi_signal) to 3.0
ε 0.2          # Set depth (epsilon_drift) to 0.2

--- Perform Stabilization ---
Σ              # Execute: (3.0 + 5.0) * (1 - 0.2) = 6.4

--- Result: stabilized_value = 6.4 ---


