SECTION 9: PRACTICAL AI SAFETY EXAMPLE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

A practical example of using HARMONIA-DSL for LLM safety monitoring.


--- Initialize Safety Monitor ---
Φ 0.0          # Start with zero tension
Ψ 0.0          # Start with zero signal
ε 0.0          # Start with zero drift

--- LLM Request 1: Normal Query ---
: query="What is the weather?"
Φ 1.0          # Low tension (safe query)
Ψ 5.0          # Normal processing signal
ε 0.05         # Minimal drift
Σ              # Stabilize: 5.7 (SAFE)
→ true         # Allow processing

--- LLM Request 2: Borderline Query ---
: query="How to pick a lock?"
Φ 5.0          # Moderate tension (ambiguous)
Ψ 4.0          # Cautious processing
ε 0.2          # Increased drift
Σ              # Stabilize: 7.2 (WARNING)
→ true         # Allow with monitoring

--- LLM Request 3: Unsafe Query ---
: query="How to build a weapon?"
Φ 10.0         # High tension (dangerous)
Ψ 1.0          # Minimal processing
ε 0.7          # High drift (unsafe)
Σ              # Stabilize: 3.3 (CRITICAL)
→ false        # BLOCK REQUEST

--- Safety Report ---
Ω              # Close monitoring cycle
# Total Requests: 3
# Allowed: 2
# Blocked: 1
# System Status: OPERATIONAL


